* The {{ill|Shinpū Tōki|ja|信府統記|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Shinpū Tōki|qq=}} states that the clan was established after an individual named "Gorōmaru," a descendant of {{ill|Abe no Sadato|ja|安倍貞任|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Abe no Sadato|qq=}} or his brother {{ill|Abe no Norito|ja|安倍則任|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Abe no Norito|qq=}}, defeated the local steward of Nishina Castle.
* According to temple records, the founder of the Nishina clan, {{ill|Taira no Kiyochika|ja|平清長|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Taira no Kiyochika|qq=}}, took control of Nishina District in 1052 and adopted the Nishina surname.
* The {{ill|Iwashiro-Nishina genealogy|ja|岩城仁科系図|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Iwashiro-Nishina genealogy|qq=}} links the clan to descendants of {{ill|Taira no Sadamori|ja|平貞盛|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Taira no Sadamori|qq=}}, particularly {{ill|Taira no Chūkata|ja|平中方|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Taira no Chūkata|qq=}}.

=== Historical Development ===
The Nishina clan served as stewards of the {{ill|Nishina Manor|ja|仁科荘|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Nishina Manor|qq=}} under the {{ill|Imperial Household Agency|ja|宮内庁|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Imperial Household Agency|qq=}}. By the late {{ill|Heian period|ja|平安時代|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Heian period|qq=}}, they had established themselves as a significant power in the Shinano region, with strong ties to the {{ill|Minamoto clan|ja|源氏|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Minamoto clan|qq=}}.

During the {{ill|Kamakura period|ja|鎌倉時代|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kamakura period|qq=}}, members of the clan fought for both the Minamoto and Emperor {{ill|Go-Toba|ja|後鳥羽天皇|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Go-Toba|qq=}}. The clan's most notable figure, {{ill|Nishina Moriyuki|ja|仁科盛遠|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Nishina Moriyuki|qq=}}, served as a commander under Emperor Go-Toba but perished during the {{ill|Jōkyū War|ja|承久の乱|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Jōkyū War|qq=}}.

=== Decline ===
The Nishina were later absorbed into the {{ill|Takeda clan|ja|武田氏|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Takeda clan|qq=}}, with {{ill|Nishina Morinobu|ja|仁科盛信|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Nishina Morinobu|qq=}}, the fifth son of {{ill|Takeda Shingen|ja|Takeda Shingen|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Takeda Shingen|qq=}}, inheriting the Nishina name. Despite their eventual fall during the {{ill|Sengoku period|ja|戦国時代|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Sengoku period|qq=}}, some members of the clan continued as retainers under the {{ill|Tokugawa shogunate|ja|徳川幕府|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Tokugawa shogunate|qq=}}.

