* According to temple records, the founder of the Nishina clan, {{ill|Taira no Kiyochika|ja|平清長|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Taira no Kiyochika|qq=|ja_comment=jawiki link invalid}}, took control of Nishina District in 1052 and adopted the Nishina surname.
* The {{ill|Iwashiro-Nishina genealogy|ja|岩城仁科系図|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Iwashiro-Nishina genealogy|qq=|ja_comment=jawiki link invalid}} links the clan to descendants of [[:en:Taira no Sadamori|Taira no Sadamori]], particularly {{ill|Taira no Chūkata|ja|平中方|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Taira no Chūkata|qq=|ja_comment=jawiki link invalid}}.

=== Historical Development ===
The Nishina clan served as stewards of the {{ill|Nishina Manor|ja|仁科荘|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Nishina Manor|qq=|1=Nishina Manor|comment=changed title based on wikidata|WD=Q85876049}} under the [[:en:Imperial Household Agency|Imperial Household Agency]]. By the late [[:en:Heian period|Heian period]], they had established themselves as a significant power in the Shinano region, with strong ties to the [[:en:Minamoto clan|Minamoto clan]].

During the [[:en:Kamakura period|Kamakura period]], members of the clan fought for both the Minamoto and Emperor [[:en:Emperor Go-Toba|Go-Toba]]. The clan's most notable figure, {{ill|Nishina Moriyuki|ja|仁科盛遠|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Nishina Moriyuki|qq=|1=Nishina Moriyuki|comment=changed title based on wikidata|WD=Q11376460}}, served as a commander under Emperor Go-Toba but perished during the [[:en:Jōkyū War|Jōkyū War]].

=== Decline ===
The Nishina were later absorbed into the [[:en:Takeda clan|Takeda clan]], with [[:en:Nishina Morinobu|Nishina Morinobu]], the fifth son of [[Takeda Shingen]]{{efn|Japanese feudal lord (1521–1573)|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Takeda Shingen|qq=|ja_comment=jawiki link invalid}}, inheriting the Nishina name. Despite their eventual fall during the {{ill|Sengoku period|ja|戦国時代|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Sengoku period|qq=|1=Sengoku Period (Japan)|comment=changed title based on wikidata|WD=Q117415390}}, some members of the clan continued as retainers under the {{ill|Tokugawa shogunate|ja|徳川幕府|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Tokugawa shogunate|qq=|ja_comment=jawiki redirects to 江戸幕府}}.

